WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.500
Sarah Chen: Morning everyone. Three topics today: the onboarding redesign, the billing bug, and the Q4 dashboard. Lina, where are we on onboarding?

2
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Lina Ferrari: The new flow is designed, five screens instead of eight. I still need to finish the empty states. I'll have the final mockups in Figma by Wednesday.

3
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Sarah Chen: Great. Omar, can your team start building once the mockups are in?

4
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Omar Haddad: Yes, but first I have to fix the billing bug. Customers on annual plans are charged twice when they upgrade. It's the top priority, I'll ship a fix by end of day tomorrow.

5
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Sarah Chen: Agreed, that one can't wait. Karim, can you pull the list of affected accounts so support can refund them?

6
00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:25.000
Karim Benali: Sure. I'll run the query this afternoon and send the list to support by Thursday at the latest.

7
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Sarah Chen: Perfect. On the dashboard: last week we decided to drop the weekly email report and keep only the live dashboard. Is everyone still fine with that?

8
00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Lina Ferrari: Fine with me.

9
00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:12.000
Karim Benali: Yes. I do need the tracking events documented though, otherwise the retention chart will be wrong. Someone should write that spec.

10
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Sarah Chen: Good point. Nobody owns that yet, so let's put it on the list and assign it next week.

11
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:46.000
Omar Haddad: One more thing, the staging database is almost full. I'll ask DevOps to increase the storage. Low priority, sometime this month.

12
00:03:50.000 --> 00:04:02.000
Sarah Chen: Noted. I'll write up the Q4 roadmap and share it with the whole team before our next sync on November 16.

13
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:14.000
Sarah Chen: Anything else? No? Thanks everyone.
